o infamous  musical police procedural pop rock and  rock it did not  Henry Simmons joining blue in its  seventh season as meta voice new partner  Baldwin Jones Henry Simmons was one-half  of a formidable team with Jones's  intensity and meta voice persistence  working in tandem to get confessions out  of skills  Simmons is currently part of the Marvel  TV universes Mack on agents of shield  you may have also caught him on shows  like Ravenswood and man up build rocked  row as PAA upstairs John Irvin bill  brock trip brought heart diversity and  subtle humor to what could have been a  thankless forgettable role prior to Blue  Rock trip was a regular on Steven Bochco  shows like total security and the doomed  cop comedy public morals these days  Brock Tripp keeps busy in the theater  world and brings the same sensitivity he  brought to Jon to his role as  psychologist dr. Bowman on TNT's major  crimes Sharon Lawrence a DA Sylvia  Costas was on the receiving end of one  of Sipowicz his most memorably profane  rants in the pilot episode of NYPD Blue  but she eventually fell for his gruff  charms and married the old lug her  murder during season six left Sipowicz  to raise their infant son alone actress  Sharon Lawrence who scored three Emmy  nominations for her role  the series in 1996 to co-star with Leah  Remini on the short-lived NBC sitcom  fired up a TV vet she's had memorable  roles on shows like Desperate Housewives  Grey's Anatomy and shameless Charlotte  Ross prior to NYPD Blue Charlotte Ross  cut her teeth in the soap opera world  and starred on the short-lived Fox  musical drama The Heights she joined the  cop drama in 2001 and made a splash when  her character detective Connie McDowell  appeared partially nude in a  controversial 2004 episode the  sweet-natured McDowell would eventually  melt grumpy ol Sipowicz his heart and  the pair married and raised kids in the  show's later seasons Ross has kept busy  on television since blue ended with  turns on shows 